Request Flow - Full Workflow:User types: app.girija.com -> Route53 -> ALB -> Target Group -> ECS Fargate TaskRoute53: User types domain. Route53 is DNS. It checks A-record (Alias) - "Where is app.girija.com?" -> It says "Go to my ALB - my-alb-123.ap-south-1.elb.amazonaws.com"ALB (Port 443/80): 
Request hits ALB Listener. Listener rule: "If path is /*, forward to Target Group ecs-tg". ALB also does SSL offloading using ACM certificate.Target Group: TG has list of your ECS Tasks IPs (10.0.1.5, 10.0.1.6). It already did Health Check on /health. Only healthy tasks get traffic.ECS Task: Your Docker container receives request on port 80/3000 and sends response back same way.What is Health Check path /health?It's a small URL your app creates just to say "I am alive". ALB hits http://10.0.1.5:80/health every 30 sec. If it gets 200 OK, task is healthy. If 3 fails, ALB marks Unhealthy and stops sending traffic.You must create this /health route in your app code.Interview Q&A for DAY 4:1. ALB vs NLB?ALB (Layer 7 - HTTP): Understands HTTP, host/path routing (/api -> one TG, /admin -> another TG). Best for your web apps. NLB (Layer 4 - TCP): Super fast, no HTTP understanding, for TCP/gaming/millions req. Not needed for you.Why ALB for HTTP? Because we need path-based routing and ACM SSL.2. What if 1 target fails health check?
ALB auto-removes that target from TG. Traffic goes only to healthy targets. User sees no error. ECS will kill unhealthy task and start new one.3. Sticky Sessions?
ALB can enable stickiness - same user always goes to same target using cookie AWSALB. Needed if your app stores session in memory. But for ECS, we keep it OFF and store session in Redis/RDS.How to say in interview (30 sec):"User hits Route53 which alias to ALB. ALB listener on 443 with ACM cert forwards to Target Group based on rule. TG health checks each ECS task on /health endpoint. If healthy, request goes to Fargate task. If one target fails 3 checks, ALB removes it."

final answer:
"User hits Route53 which alias to ALB. ALB listener on 443 with ACM cert forwards to Target Group based on rule. TG health checks each ECS task on /health endpoint. If healthy, request goes to Fargate task. If one target fails 3 checks, ALB removes it.

